    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-χολέω</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-χολία</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρό-χολος</span></b> , v. sub <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκραχ-</span>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδών</span></b> ,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όνος</span>, ἡ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wart with a thin neck</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				3.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fab.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.64
			</span></i>, etc.; distinguished from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρμήκια,
					τά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				4.15
			</span></i> (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-δάνη</span></b> 
			<u>Gloss.</u>, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-δόνη</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>, 
				Dim.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-δόνιον</span></b> )
			<u>Gloss.</u>: hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρο-χορδονώδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
				<i>troubled with warts</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				47
			</span></i>.</div>
